# What the boundary lint (boundary.mjs) lets through today: one line per file and
# rule, `<path> <rule> <count>`, sorted, with an optional ` # why`. The count is
# exact, so this list only shrinks: a slice lowers or deletes the lines of the
# files it changes (`node scripts/loops/boundary.mjs --write` rewrites the counts).
.github/workflows/ci.yml project-to-core 1
package.json project-to-core 4
risa.json project-to-core 1 # hooks.lease is the core's lease.sh hold, which the app's browser lease helper runs: its path changes at the move
